# help.psv -- how each program is asked for its own help.  name|command|note
#
# One line per program, written by somebody who has just run it.  The
# command is what a reader types to get the help -- `-?' is the OS-9
# convention and not universal.  `none' means the program prints no help
# of its own, and the note says what the card shows instead.  A leading
# `load X;' or `chd X;' is hidden setup; `<< a\rb' feeds standard input.
# tools/helpcap.py captures every command here into docs/help/<name>.txt,
# whole, and the gate `cards carry real help text' checks the captures
# against this table.  tools/help-backlog.txt lists what is not here yet.
roff|roff -?|
bm|bm -?|
cdiff|cdiff -?|
cookie|cookie -?|
cursive|cursive -?|
diff|diff -?|
diff_1.1|diff_1.1 -?|
deton|deton -?|
fcomp|fcomp -?|
gothic|none|it draws whatever it is given, a `-?' included: `gothic word' sets the word, and `-h' halves the height
grep|grep -?|
jargon|jargon -?|
lout|lout -u|
sort|sort -?|
soundex|none|a filter with no options: one word a line on standard input, one Soundex key a line out
speech|speech -?|
what|none|it takes no options and ignores its arguments; run it and it prints its table
