xkermit|xkermit -?|
ckermit|ckermit -h|
kermit_cio|kermit_cio -?|
finger|finger -?|
net|none|it takes the name of a startup file and no options; `help' at its `net>' prompt lists its commands
osknet|none|it takes its commands at its own prompt; DOC/osknet has the guide
msntp|none|it takes the address of a time server and no help flag
atp|none|it takes no options: it reads atprc or .atprc from the data directory
infoxpress|none|it takes no options: it opens its serial device and waits for the host
uucp|uucp -?|
uucico|uucico -?|
uuxqt|none|it takes no options; it looks for `procs' before it starts
uuname|uuname -?|
uulog|uulog -?|
uuclean|uuclean -?|
fileserv|none|it takes no options and prints nothing; it answers the requests waiting in the spool
fixtext|fixtext -?|
wn|none|inetd gives it its options and the request arrives on standard input; there is no help flag
wndex|wndex -?|
inetd|inetd -?|
inetdc|none|inetd forks it; it takes no options and carries no message text
authwn|none|wn invokes it per request; it takes no options
vmod_trap|none|a trap-handler module, not a program: `load' it before rxmod and txmod
screen|none|-v prints its version; it has no help flag, and it wants a $HOME/.screens directory
